{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md | sed -n '912,942p;1880,1918p;1988,2056p'; rg -n 'spawn-child|defn run|advance-installs' src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc; git diff --stat 2>/dev/null; rg -n 'phase :running|:phase :parked' test/yin/vm/ucf/handoff_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"   912\t  checks the linker applied at delivery (`yin.vm.linker.md` sections\n   913\t  5 and 9): the image is well formed, hashes to the address it is\n   914\t  delivered under, and is the image the manifest names. A failure is\n   915\t  `:yin.k/undecodable` naming the entry's response.\n   916\t- `:yin.k/phase` is `:running` or `:parked`, the two phases in which\n   917\t  a child is live. A `:parked` phase requires a child body of kind\n   918\t  `:blocked`; a `:running` phase requires a child body of kind\n   919\t  `:halted`, a halt the scheduler has not yet validated. `:loading`\n   920\t  has no child to carry, and `:validated`, `:linked` and `:refused`\n   921\t  are over. Any other value or pairing is `:yin.k/undecodable`.\n   922\t- The resumer restores the child's carried state into the fresh\n   923\t  child before the scheduler may step it. The fresh child is a\n   924\t  template for the receiver's coordinates only: it does not run the\n   925\t  module's initialization again, and nothing replays the link\n   926\t  request.\n   927\t- The child is a whole body of 7.2.1 in the version of its holder,\n   928\t  with its own frames, parked records, stores, cells, code, and\n   929\t  nested installs. It is validated by the same grammar in the child\n   930\t  role, recursively and with its root's context (7.2.1), before\n   931\t  anything of the parent is restored.\n   932\t- Every live child travels, waited on or not, and no child steps\n   933\t  while its task is exporting (7.7.4). A child that cannot be\n   934\t  exported refuses the parent's export with the child's own outcome;\n   935\t  a child that cannot be lowered refuses the parent's lower. No\n   936\t  parent is published or restored over a child that did not cross.\n   937\t- An `:install` pending whose name has no entry refuses the lift as\n   938\t  `:yin.k/non-portable`, kind `:incomplete-install`, before\n   939\t  publication; a body carrying such a pending is\n   940\t  `:yin.k/undecodable`. An obligation a carried child will bind on\n   941\t  completion is discharged by that child, not reported missing.\n   942\t- The waiter list is not carried. The waiters of a child are exactly\n  1880\t  by the attribution the composition supplies (`dao.lease.md`,\n  1881\t  *Composition duties*). An envelope whose attributed author is not\n  1882\t  the holder that the binding of `L` names is a fact about that\n  1883\t  author: it is defective.\n  1884\t\n  1885\t**Defective envelopes.** A defective envelope commits no effect and\n  1886\tcreates no dedup record. It yields no admission outcome: an outcome\n  1887\twould be attributed to the holder its fields claim, and those fields\n  1888\tare exactly what cannot be trusted. The consumer instead appends one\n  1889\tstructured diagnostic to its diagnostic stream:\n  1890\t\n  1891\t```clojure\n  1892\t{:yin.k/diagnostic :yin.k/defective-envelope\n  1893\t :yin.k/defect     :malformed       ; closed, below\n  1894\t :yin.k/target     i                ; the boundary's stream identity\n  1895\t :yin.k/author     a                ; resolved attribution, if any\n  1896\t :yin.k/claimed    {...}}           ; readable envelope fields\n  1897\t```\n  1898\t\n  1899\t- `:yin.k/defect` is one of `:malformed` (a missing key, an unknown\n  1900\t  dispatch value, an integer out of kind or range), `:unbound-lease`\n  1901\t  (no valid binding for the incarnation), `:wrong-author` (the\n  1902\t  attributed author is not the bound holder), and `:foreign-op-id`\n  1903\t  (the id fails the scope check below).\n  1904\t- `:yin.k/claimed` holds whichever of `:yin.k/incarnation`,\n  1905\t  `:yin.k/epoch` and `:yin.k/op-id` could be read, as claims. They\n  1906\t  are nested so that no reader correlating on a top-level op id can\n  1907\t  take the diagnostic for an answer. The payload is never echoed.\n  1908\t- The map carries neither `:yin.k/admission` nor `:yin.k/status`. A\n  1909\t  driver discharges nothing and ends nothing on a diagnostic.\n  1910\t\n  1911\t**Intent.** Intent is the vector `[effect-kind target-identity\n  1912\tpayload]`: the keyword naming the boundary's operation, the target's\n  1913\t`:dao.stream/identity`, and the envelope's `:yin.k/value`. This\n  1914\tamendment enrolls one effect kind, `:yin.k/append`, a stream append;\n  1915\tevery write the reference machine retains is one. Two intents are\n  1916\tequal when their canonical bytes are equal. FFI and link correlation\n  1917\tids are inside the payload and are compared with it; they are not\n  1918\toperation ids.\n  1988\tby one atomic transition against the authority's admission resource\n  1989\t(7.7.5). The checks run in this order and the first to fail decides\n  1990\tthe outcome (7.9):\n  1991\t\n  1992\t1. *Authority.* The authority the consumer is enrolled with must be\n  1993\t   readable. If it is unreachable, if its ledger for the occurrence\n  1994\t   that `L` is bound to is not recoverable, or if that occurrence\n  1995\t   is exhausted, the outcome is `:suspended`. An occurrence\n  1996\t   quarantined after an intent conflict (below) answers the same.\n  1997\t2. *Binding.* `L` has a valid binding, and the envelope's attributed\n  1998\t   author is the holder it names. Otherwise the envelope is\n  1999\t   defective: a diagnostic, and no outcome.\n  2000\t3. *Tenure.* The bound occurrence is open, `L` is its active lease,\n  2001\t   and `e` equals its current epoch, else `:stale`. Staleness is\n  2002\t   decided before the dedup record is consulted: a stale envelope is\n  2003\t   refused even when a record for its id exists.\n  2004\t4. *Scope.* An operation assigned during the current occurrence\n  2005\t   names that occurrence. An inherited operation must occur among\n  2006\t   the retained pending operations of the authoritative checkpoint\n  2007\t   granted to the holder, including its install children, and its\n  2008\t   occurrence must be an ancestor through authoritative completion\n  2009\t   records. Membership is derived from the accepted checkpoint, the\n  2010\t   body the authority admitted for the granted occurrence; no\n  2011\t   ancestry index and no pending-id index is stored. An id that\n  2012\t   fails is defective, `:foreign-op-id`. If the accepted checkpoint\n  2013\t   cannot be read, the outcome is `:suspended`.\n  2014\t5. *Dedup.* With a record for the id: equal intent answers\n  2015\t   `:replayed` with the recorded result and commits nothing;\n  2016\t   different intent answers `:intent-conflict` and commits nothing.\n  2017\t   With no record: the effect, its result, and the record\n  2018\t   `{op-id -> {intent result}}` commit together, and the outcome is\n  2019\t   `:committed`.\n  2020\t\n  2021\t**Results and uncertainty.** The recorded result is the effect's\n  2022\tdefinitive outcome, as plain data; for a stream append it is the\n  2023\ttarget's DaoStream outcome map, unchanged. A terminal refusal is a\n  2024\tresult, recorded and replayed unchanged, but only when the atomic\n  2025\tadmission boundary itself establishes it. An outcome that leaves the\n  2026\teffect unknown, such as a `:dao.stream/transport-error` from a\n  2027\ttransport whose failures are not declared clean, is not a result:\n  2028\tnothing is recorded, no admission outcome is produced, the id stays\n  2029\tretained, and the write is reconciled by retrying the same envelope.\n  2030\tBackpressure is likewise no commitment: it is the writer path's own\n  2031\t`:dao.stream/full`.\n  2032\t\n  2033\t**One dedup namespace.** The dedup records form one logical namespace\n  2034\tper arbitration admission resource, across every enrolled target that\n  2035\ttakes part in the guarantee, keyed by the operation id alone. Target\n  2036\tidentity is part of the intent, never of the key. So a replay that\n  2037\tdiverges and sends an id to another target meets the first target's\n  2038\trecord and answers `:intent-conflict`. A consumer that cannot join\n  2039\tthat atomic resource keeps no private table in its place: it cannot\n  2040\tclaim the cross-target guarantee, and its stream is not enrolled.\n  2041\t\n  2042\t**Enrollment.** That a target stream is enrolled is an attributed\n  2043\tfact of the authority on the arbitration medium, keyed by the target\n  2044\tstream's identity. No body carries it. M-next C defines its schema\n  2045\tand ensures that a change of enrollment cannot alter the protection\n  2046\tof an operation already retained under an id.\n  2047\t\n  2048\t**Completion and the successor chain.** Completion (7.7.5) establishes\n  2049\ta single acyclic chain. The authority accepts at most one successor\n  2050\tper predecessor and one predecessor per successor. The successor's\n  2051\toccurrence is fresh, its `:yin.k/origin` names the predecessor and\n  2052\tthe lease that ran it, and its `:yin.k/arbitration` identity is the\n  2053\tpredecessor's, unchanged. Only that accepted completion is an edge:\n  2054\ta published successor or a resumed report the authority did not\n  2055\taccept is an orphan, and no ancestry runs through it. A closed\n  2056\toccurrence receives no further grant.\n1087:(defn- spawn-child\n1250:(defn- advance-installs\n1260:    (let [[child state] (spawn-child state module-name response)]\n1376:        advance-installs)))\n1658:(defn run-loop\n docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md                   | 108 ++-\n docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md                |  50 +-\n .../design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md | 792 ++++++++++++++++++++-\n 3 files changed, 908 insertions(+), 42 deletions(-)\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
